; expect 42
; The operators no other conformance case exercises.
;
; Measured over the 90 cases of this directory before this one was
; added: `>>`, `%`, `|` and `^` appeared in ZERO of them, `>=` in one,
; `<=` in two, and only two cases compared floats at all. A codegen
; mistake in any of those - the wrong LLVM predicate, `lshr` where
; `ashr` is meant, `urem` for `srem` - compiled cleanly, ran, and was
; caught by nothing. It would also survive a re-bless of every golden
; in the repository, because the whole corpus that could contradict it
; was silent.
;
; An adversarial pass over `check-bootstrap.sh` found this by getting
; three separately-wrong compilers past a ladder that reaches
; `stage2 == stage3` and passes 90 conformance cases: the fixpoint says
; the compiler reproduces itself, not that it is right, and the corpus
; only reaches as far as the fixtures go.
;
; Drilled rather than assumed: a compiler built with one token changed
; in `codegen.ax` - `(if (strEq nm ">>") "ashr")` to `"lshr"` - answers
; 26 here instead of 42, and 140 on `320-mangle.ax` exactly as before.
; The missing 16 names the term that broke, and the untouched case is
; the blind spot this file exists to close.
;
; Every term is chosen for a shape the compiler cannot check by
; self-consistency, and the total is a sum of powers of two so that a
; single wrong term names itself in the exit status:
;
;   1   fcmp oeq, on floats                    (== 1.5 1.5)
;   2   fcmp one, taking the FALSE branch      (!= 1.5 1.5)
;   4   fcmp oge at the boundary               (>= 2.5 2.5)
;   8   fcmp ole at the boundary               (<= 2.5 2.5)
;  16   ashr, not lshr: -8 >> 1 stays negative (>> (- 0 8) 1)
;   2   srem                                   (% 17 5)
;   3   or                                     (| 1 2)
;   6   xor                                    (^ 5 3)
(:: main Int)

(fn (main)
  (+
    (if (== 1.5 1.5)
      1
      0
    )    (+
      (if (!= 1.5 1.5)
        0
        2
      )      (+
        (if (>= 2.5 2.5)
          4
          0
        )        (+
          (if (<= 2.5 2.5)
            8
            0
          )          (+
            (if (< (>> (- 0 8) 1) 0)
              16
              0
            )            (+ (% 17 5) (+ (| 1 2) (^ 5 3)))
          )
        )
      )
    )
  )
)
